Optional 2x VBlank IRQ10 source for Namco_System_10_MiSTer (base 8a8c283)

OSD Hardware > "IRQ10 (Input)": 100Hz (default, unchanged, = MAME) / 2xVBlank.
2xVBlank sends the same I/O IRQ10 pulse (int status bit 3) at 1/4 and 3/4 of the
last measured frame length after each VBlank rising edge: two per frame
(~119.88/s at 59.94 Hz). The 100 Hz counter keeps running; only its pulse is
gated. The CD-ROM IRQ10 path is unchanged.

Why: the real-board IRQ10 source is unknown (MAME: TODO). Mr. Driller 2 / G
store IN1 on every other IRQ10, so 100 Hz gives 50 input samples/s (beats
against 59.94 fps); 2x VBlank gives exactly one sample per frame. On our core
(Driller 2/G, Gamshara, Star Trigon) it was smoother and matched real-board
rapid-fire videos. Other games (Taiko CD IRQ10, guns, NFL, ...) were NOT
tested - that's why it is an option and 100Hz stays the default.

Files: rtl/s10_io.sv (+irq10_vbl, +vblank inputs), Namco_S10.sv (OSD bit 65,
psx_vbl), sim/system/tb_s10.template.vhd (new ports tied to '0').
Unit test: tb_s10_io_irq10.sv (ModelSim/Questa: vlog -sv s10_io.sv
tb_s10_io_irq10.sv; vsim -c tb_irq10 -do "run -all") -> PASS
(100 Hz spacing 338688 clk; 2x VBlank offsets 1/4,3/4 of frame +-2 clk, 2 per
frame; CD INTRQ still raises IRQ10).
Background: docs/rapid-fire-irq-eng.md of the namcos10 core.
Apply: git apply namco_s10-irq10-2xvblank.patch

